<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold rates seen rising on Ramadan demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold rates seen rising on Ramadan demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold rates are expected to rise on higher demand for gold jewellery in the Moslem fasting month of Ramadan, the Eid al-Fitr religious feast and the March-April wedding season, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Silver rates are seen unchanged as there is little demand for silver jewellery, one dealer said.</p>
<p>							 Sunday   Dec 30</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grammes 5,110    5,263</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   7,286    7,286</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
